    {
      "topLeftX": 96,
      "topLeftY": 374,
      "bottomRightX": 389,
      "bottomRightY": 436,
      "content": "Header bytes are loaded into the header register IC's 19,20 when HWE=0 (Header write enable). Header reading by the CPU is accomplished with HRE=0, IORD=0 and SEL4=0. The CPU can then determine if the header is from the desired data block.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 97,
      "topLeftY": 446,
      "bottomRightX": 166,
      "bottomRightY": 460,
      "content": "# Byte counter",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 96,
      "topLeftY": 464,
      "bottomRightX": 389,
      "bottomRightY": 537,
      "content": "The byte counter uses 4 counters, IC's 31,32,36,38. It generates addresses for the descrambler EPROM and the RAM. The byte counter must be synchronised with the blocks. At the end of each sync pattern the counter is reset by SYN and so is rapidly pulled into lock. RDY indicates to the CPU that 3 blocks (3 x 2352) blocks are in the RAM.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 97,
      "topLeftY": 547,
      "bottomRightX": 196,
      "bottomRightY": 561,
      "content": "# RDY (ready signal)",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 96,
      "topLeftY": 565,
      "bottomRightX": 389,
      "bottomRightY": 615,
      "content": "RDY informs the CPU that 3 blocks are in the RAM. RDY is generated when TCNT(Terminate count ) occurs ( 3 x 2352-1) from IC 35. The RDY circuit is built around IC's14,13 it is reset by RES.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 97,
      "topLeftY": 626,
      "bottomRightX": 302,
      "bottomRightY": 639,
      "content": "# Read/write of header register and RAM",
